# CODEOWNERS — required reviewer protection for ADR-enforced surfaces.
#
# Why this file exists:
#   Per ADR-011 release-gate-arbiter STRIDE co-sign Tampering addendum #3,
#   the fitness functions that enforce notification suppression cannot be
#   modified in the same PR as a violation. Without CODEOWNERS, a single
#   reviewer could approve a PR that both adds a forbidden opt-in AND
#   disables the test that would have caught it. CODEOWNERS lifts the
#   bar to two-reviewer approval for these protected files.
#
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# All paths are relative to repo root. Patterns are evaluated top-to-bottom;
# the LAST matching pattern wins (so put generic rules first, specific later).
#
# IMPORTANT: GitHub requires the named users / teams to have write access
# to the repo for CODEOWNERS rules to be enforced. The team handles below
# are placeholders; replace with real GitHub usernames or @Delta-Crown-Org/<team>
# slugs once the org has the teams created.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owner — applies if no later rule matches.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                       @t-granlund

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Architecture fitness functions — the ADR enforcement layer.
# Every test in this directory enforces an architectural invariant from an
# ADR. Modifying them MUST require two-reviewer approval per ADR-011.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tests/architecture/                    @t-granlund @Delta-Crown-Org/security
/tests/architecture/test_notification_suppression.py  @t-granlund @Delta-Crown-Org/security

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADRs — the decisions register. Editing an accepted ADR is a governance
# action, not a code change. Two-reviewer approval required.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/docs/sharepoint-pnp-spec/decisions/    @t-granlund @Delta-Crown-Org/security
/docs/sharepoint-pnp-spec/NOTIFICATION-SUPPRESSION-PLAYBOOK.md  @t-granlund @Delta-Crown-Org/security

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI/CD workflows — the deploy surface. Tampering with these bypasses the
# fitness functions; two-reviewer required.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/                     @t-granlund @Delta-Crown-Org/security
/dce-mockup/ci-cd/workflows/            @t-granlund @Delta-Crown-Org/security

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CODEOWNERS itself — meta-rule. Without this line, anyone could rewrite
# CODEOWNERS to remove the protections above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @t-granlund @Delta-Crown-Org/security

